00:21:18.311 --> 00:21:21.129
her slaves that that was the plan.

00:21:21.129 --> 00:21:22.448
She said, she didn't want to equality,

00:21:22.448 --> 00:21:25.406
she wanted revenge, by the way--

00:21:25.406 --> 00:21:26.612
- It's nice when they're honest about it.

00:21:26.612 --> 00:21:28.244
- She was completely
honest about it, I say,

00:21:28.244 --> 00:21:30.521
I'm being careful about
because she's a mother

00:21:30.521 --> 00:21:34.619
and she was at a house
party in London last year.

00:21:34.619 --> 00:21:36.506
And she was shot in the head.

00:21:36.506 --> 00:21:38.736
And immediately some politicians,

00:21:38.736 --> 00:21:42.323
including the Black former
shadow home secretary said,

00:21:42.323 --> 00:21:43.422
"It's appalling this poor young woman

00:21:43.422 --> 00:21:45.246
"Is been gunned down for her beliefs."

00:21:45.246 --> 00:21:49.899
She was gunned down by a
gang of Black young men

00:21:49.899 --> 00:21:53.372
who were shooting at a
house party she was at.

00:21:53.372 --> 00:21:54.758
So again,

00:21:54.758 --> 00:21:57.530
we have these kind of just
totally false narratives,

00:21:57.530 --> 00:22:00.566
you import the BLM thing to Oxford,

00:22:00.566 --> 00:22:01.399
- Yeah.

00:22:01.399 --> 00:22:02.458
- In England.

00:22:02.458 --> 00:22:05.285
And then you have this horrible radical,

00:22:05.285 --> 00:22:08.002
and then something terrible
happens then all of it,

00:22:08.002 --> 00:22:12.335
all of it is spun through
the thing of white racism.

00:22:14.669 --> 00:22:16.176
- Let's do a little sidebar for a moment,

00:22:16.176 --> 00:22:18.090
'cause just as you spun
that story together

00:22:18.090 --> 00:22:19.894
and all the lies and everything else

00:22:19.894 --> 00:22:23.348
over the last couple years are you,

00:22:23.348 --> 00:22:26.703
to me if someone managed
to stay roughly sane,

00:22:26.703 --> 00:22:28.859
like they're good in
my book that's been my,

00:22:28.859 --> 00:22:32.016
like basic temperature
guide on this thing,

00:22:32.016 --> 00:22:33.193
you didn't have to get everything right,

00:22:33.193 --> 00:22:34.026
none of us did,

00:22:34.026 --> 00:22:36.515
but if you sort of said roughly sane,

00:22:36.515 --> 00:22:38.759
do you sympathize with the
people that really lost it over

00:22:38.759 --> 00:22:40.794
the last couple years because
of exactly what you just

00:22:40.794 --> 00:22:41.696
explained right there,

00:22:41.696 --> 00:22:44.072
there is such a cacophony of nonsense

00:22:44.072 --> 00:22:45.304
being spun at all of us all the time,

00:22:45.304 --> 00:22:47.746
it's extremely difficult,

00:22:47.746 --> 00:22:48.813
and people don't have the time

00:22:48.813 --> 00:22:50.331
siphon through all the craziness?

00:22:50.331 --> 00:22:52.331
- Yeah, I do understand.

00:22:53.169 --> 00:22:54.533
And I have to use the word

00:22:54.533 --> 00:22:57.173
check my privilege in a certain way.

00:22:57.173 --> 00:22:59.880
My privilege is that I'm a writer,

00:22:59.880 --> 00:23:03.130
I get to say what I think all the time.

00:23:04.181 --> 00:23:06.153
- But that's not just the privilege,

00:23:06.153 --> 00:23:08.387
it's also you do put your neck out there,

00:23:08.387 --> 00:23:09.220
I mean, it's not,

00:23:09.220 --> 00:23:10.053
- Yeah.

00:23:10.053 --> 00:23:11.761
It's a privilege to a degree, but you say,

00:23:11.761 --> 00:23:12.594
- Sure.

00:23:12.594 --> 00:23:13.427
- No dangerous things or--

00:23:13.427 --> 00:23:14.260
- But I mean,

00:23:14.260 --> 00:23:17.069
but I say it because I
think that therefore,

00:23:17.069 --> 00:23:19.566
so my own attitude is a bit
different to some other people

00:23:19.566 --> 00:23:23.570
because I think what is worse
for people is when they see

00:23:23.570 --> 00:23:26.430
lies and they just have no outlet for it.

00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:27.263
- Yeah.

00:23:27.263 --> 00:23:29.596
- They just, I think there
is enormous frustration

00:23:29.596 --> 00:23:30.463
brewing everywhere,

00:23:30.463 --> 00:23:34.599
we've been through a couple
of really difficult years.

00:23:34.599 --> 00:23:37.291
So I do have sympathy with it.

00:23:37.291 --> 00:23:39.780
My sympathy for that is not endless

00:23:39.780 --> 00:23:41.108
I don't have sympathy for the people,

00:23:41.108 --> 00:23:43.512
who've who now believe that absolutely

00:23:43.512 --> 00:23:44.829
everything is a conspiracy,

00:23:44.829 --> 00:23:47.858
and believe that they've
seen through everything.

00:23:47.858 --> 00:23:48.838
- Yeah.

00:23:48.838 --> 00:23:50.851
- And all, I've not got
much sympathy with that

00:23:50.851 --> 00:23:52.518
because I mean, you,

00:23:53.392 --> 00:23:56.133
it's not just that you,
it's not that you have to,

00:23:56.133 --> 00:23:59.210
you should find things to trust in,

00:23:59.210 --> 00:24:01.542
you can't be completely cynical,

00:24:01.542 --> 00:24:03.306
you should find things that you know

00:24:03.306 --> 00:24:05.436
to be true and hold on to them.

00:24:05.436 --> 00:24:07.634
- Right, if you're the one
guy who knows what's going on,

00:24:07.634 --> 00:24:09.829
you probably have an issue.

00:24:09.829 --> 00:24:11.661
- I worry there's a lot of that.

00:24:11.661 --> 00:24:12.494
- Yeah.

00:24:12.494 --> 00:24:16.356
- There's a lot of
autodidacticism really like,

00:24:16.356 --> 00:24:19.485
we inevitably we educate
ourselves in areas of a lot,

00:24:19.485 --> 00:24:22.466
but I am suspicious of the people

00:24:22.466 --> 00:24:23.775
who go from being,

00:24:23.775 --> 00:24:27.702
experts on Afghanistan
to experts on vaccines,

00:24:27.702 --> 00:24:31.640
to experts on Ukraine, to experts on, I...

00:24:31.640 --> 00:24:33.607
- Everyone's an expert
in Ukraine right now.

00:24:33.607 --> 00:24:34.440
- They are amazing.

00:24:34.440 --> 00:24:36.661
- These people who couldn't
tie their shoes together.

00:24:36.661 --> 00:24:37.494
- Yeah.

00:24:37.494 --> 00:24:39.914
- And suddenly everyone shows everything.

00:24:39.914 --> 00:24:40.747
- Yeah.

00:24:40.747 --> 00:24:42.092
- About this nation that nobody would--

00:24:42.092 --> 00:24:45.048
- Hold my shoes I've gotta go back

00:24:45.048 --> 00:24:47.141
to analyzing Afghanistan next week,

00:24:47.141 --> 00:24:51.642
if anything kicks off there (laughing).

00:24:51.642 --> 00:24:53.389
I think in a way this is because politics

00:24:53.389 --> 00:24:55.270
has become a kind of hobby,

00:24:55.270 --> 00:24:57.295
it's more than a hobby, a hobby

00:24:57.295 --> 00:24:59.088
and then something more for a lot people,

00:24:59.088 --> 00:25:00.958
it's carrying an awful lot of weight.

00:25:00.958 --> 00:25:01.791
- Yeah.

00:25:01.791 --> 00:25:03.708
So we go from like the,

00:25:04.621 --> 00:25:07.415
the way it travels and it
jumps across ponds and then odd

00:25:07.415 --> 00:25:09.450
things are happening in England.

00:25:09.450 --> 00:25:11.683
But what about the way it also shifts?

00:25:11.683 --> 00:25:14.994
So we had two years of
everything was about race,

00:25:14.994 --> 00:25:17.766
but right now, as we sit here,
everything's about gender.

00:25:17.766 --> 00:25:20.285
And we'll talk more
about that in a second,

00:25:20.285 --> 00:25:22.485
but that sort of thing, that

00:25:22.485 --> 00:25:26.533
it seems to be guided in a
way that that doesn't seem

00:25:26.533 --> 00:25:29.789
totally coincidental to me that
the way it actually shifts,

00:25:29.789 --> 00:25:32.000
like we're not doing race
that much in America right

00:25:32.000 --> 00:25:34.772
this moment, it really does
seem to be more about gender.

00:25:34.772 --> 00:25:37.863
Race will come back and then
gender will come back and then

00:25:37.863 --> 00:25:39.046
climate will come and.

00:25:39.046 --> 00:25:39.879
- Yeah.

00:25:39.879 --> 00:25:40.712
- And everything else.

00:25:40.712 --> 00:25:41.865
- By the way, I mean, that's sort of way

00:25:41.865 --> 00:25:43.115
with climate is another one,

00:25:43.115 --> 00:25:43.948
I mean

00:25:43.948 --> 00:25:45.942
I listed this recently in a piece

00:25:45.942 --> 00:25:50.155
before the Ukraine crisis,
we had the COVID crisis.

00:25:50.155 --> 00:25:52.445
And I mean, literally
Dr. Fauci disappeared,

00:25:52.445 --> 00:25:54.207
the moment that the
Russian tanks were all--

00:25:54.207 --> 00:25:56.989
- It was incredible
they couldn't find him.

00:25:56.989 --> 00:25:59.031
- And then before that we had the,

00:25:59.031 --> 00:26:00.755
what did we have for the Corona crisis?

00:26:00.755 --> 00:26:02.359
Well we had the racist crisis,

00:26:02.359 --> 00:26:03.630
we had the Trump crisis,

00:26:03.630 --> 00:26:04.774
We had the Brexit crisis,

00:26:04.774 --> 00:26:06.820
oh we had the climate crisis.

00:26:06.820 --> 00:26:10.129
I like everything cannot be a crisis,

00:26:10.129 --> 00:26:12.537
everything cannot be you can't live at

00:26:12.537 --> 00:26:14.537
that level of hectoring.

00:26:15.965 --> 00:26:17.676
And of all of those,

00:26:17.676 --> 00:26:19.996
one of the ones I have
the the least time for

00:26:19.996 --> 00:26:23.627
is the other people who shout
about the climate crisis.

00:26:23.627 --> 00:26:25.797
There are things that
are important to address,

00:26:25.797 --> 00:26:26.816
but when they present it

00:26:26.816 --> 00:26:29.388
as they did of the
recent summit in Glasgow,

00:26:29.388 --> 00:26:31.096
one minute left to save the planet,

00:26:31.096 --> 00:26:33.892
I think you are doing
something pretty wicked

00:26:33.892 --> 00:26:35.607
now because you are,

00:26:35.607 --> 00:26:38.177
you are making assertions
and whipping people up into

00:26:38.177 --> 00:26:41.088
fervours that are not able to be answered.

00:26:41.088 --> 00:26:43.129
- I mean, AOC told us
we got 12 years left,

00:26:43.129 --> 00:26:44.844
that was about three years ago,

00:26:44.844 --> 00:26:45.677
- I mean.

00:26:45.677 --> 00:26:46.510
- We're running outta time man.

00:26:46.510 --> 00:26:48.120
- Prince Charles said 12 years,

00:26:48.120 --> 00:26:49.453
20 years ago so.

00:26:50.658 --> 00:26:52.378
- So we're gonna be okay, is
that what you're telling me?

00:26:52.378 --> 00:26:54.279
But that is one it's that in some ways,

00:26:54.279 --> 00:26:56.096
do you feel like that's the
hardest one to talk about?

00:26:56.096 --> 00:26:57.702
I mean look you spent years talking

00:26:57.702 --> 00:27:00.001
about Islamism and Gehad,

00:27:00.001 --> 00:27:02.599
that was obviously very
hard to talk about,

00:27:02.599 --> 00:27:04.850
but we've sort of shifted
off that now that's sort of

00:27:04.850 --> 00:27:06.581
shifted, we can talk about race,

00:27:06.581 --> 00:27:07.414
we can talk about gender,

00:27:07.414 --> 00:27:09.148
but there's something about the
climate one where it's like,

00:27:09.148 --> 00:27:12.426
you feel like your whole
career could just go like that,

00:27:12.426 --> 00:27:13.915
if you talk about it.

00:27:13.915 --> 00:27:16.874
- Could do I mean, it's not
something I do very much on,

00:27:16.874 --> 00:27:19.752
but I just note that the,

00:27:19.752 --> 00:27:21.604
it seems to be one of the fallback things.

00:27:21.604 --> 00:27:23.442
If other crises are not high

00:27:23.442 --> 00:27:24.990
and hot enough at the moment we

00:27:24.990 --> 00:27:27.182
fall back onto the climate crisis

00:27:27.182 --> 00:27:29.728
and again I'm not saying
that there aren't things

00:27:29.728 --> 00:27:32.872
to address but just the
way in which this is sold

00:27:32.872 --> 00:27:34.606
to the public seems to be

00:27:34.606 --> 00:27:38.273
highly deranging, I
mean you're telling kids

00:27:39.429 --> 00:27:42.347
that they might not make adulthood,

00:27:42.347 --> 00:27:45.180
and that's a terrible thing to do.

00:27:46.277 --> 00:27:49.944
And you would only do it
if you're 100% certain,

00:27:49.944 --> 00:27:51.536
that was the case.

00:27:51.536 --> 00:27:53.404
And they're not.

00:27:53.404 --> 00:27:55.274
- Well, they would tell you they are,

00:27:55.274 --> 00:27:56.477
but they really--

00:27:56.477 --> 00:27:57.310
- If they were,

00:27:57.310 --> 00:27:58.367
they would actually be
doing something else.

00:27:58.367 --> 00:28:00.371
- Exactly, exactly.

00:28:00.371 --> 00:28:03.043
- They'd be like living as
people do when they think the

00:28:03.043 --> 00:28:04.678
plane's about to crash.

00:28:04.678 --> 00:28:07.185
- Let's shift to China a little bit,

00:28:07.185 --> 00:28:09.574
because it seems like everything
in the world is sort of

00:28:09.574 --> 00:28:12.115
being driven by China.

00:28:12.115 --> 00:28:14.978
And yet I don't sense that we
have as many China experts at

00:28:14.978 --> 00:28:18.598
the moment as we have Ukraine
experts, will they shift soon?

00:28:18.598 --> 00:28:19.431
- There will be shifting.

00:28:19.431 --> 00:28:21.233
- Do you sense they're
making the move to shift.

00:28:21.233 --> 00:28:22.400
- Yeah, they'll absolutely be shifting.

00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:25.029
- What's the basic way we should frame a

00:28:25.029 --> 00:28:26.558
China conversation?

00:28:26.558 --> 00:28:27.391
- Well as

00:28:27.391 --> 00:28:30.102
I do an interview in this because I say,

00:28:30.102 --> 00:28:31.409
what's the rest of the world doing,

00:28:31.409 --> 00:28:33.623
whilst we're doing this to ourselves.

00:28:33.623 --> 00:28:36.627
'Cause if you go to Beijing
and you look back at us,

00:28:36.627 --> 00:28:38.537
and I often find that my books come

00:28:38.537 --> 00:28:40.870
from looking back my society

00:28:42.331 --> 00:28:45.820
from another place and
somebody said to me recently,

00:28:45.820 --> 00:28:47.468
how would you define the West?

00:28:47.468 --> 00:28:48.301
And I was like well,

00:28:48.301 --> 00:28:52.088
one thing is, you know what
it is when you're not in it,

00:28:52.088 --> 00:28:53.068
like when you are in Beijing,

00:28:53.068 --> 00:28:54.382
you're not in the West,

00:28:54.382 --> 00:28:55.215
if you're in Tokyo,

00:28:55.215 --> 00:28:57.132
you're not in the West.

00:28:58.190 --> 00:29:00.115
And one of the things I say is like,

00:29:00.115 --> 00:29:02.229
if you look at what we
are doing from places

00:29:02.229 --> 00:29:04.623
like China or Moscow,

00:29:04.623 --> 00:29:07.073
it does look very
strange and you would get

00:29:07.073 --> 00:29:09.479
an odd picture of us.

00:29:09.479 --> 00:29:11.108
So among other things I said well,

00:29:11.108 --> 00:29:13.147
what are the Chinese doing whilst

00:29:13.147 --> 00:29:16.554
we're obsessing about social justice?

00:29:16.554 --> 00:29:18.082
Or what are the Russians doing whilst

00:29:18.082 --> 00:29:21.651
we're obsessing about these things?

00:29:21.651 --> 00:29:23.850
And the China thing in
particular is just fascinating

00:29:23.850 --> 00:29:27.552
because there's no
scenario in which Russia

00:29:27.552 --> 00:29:32.156
would overtake America in
global leadership terms.

00:29:32.156 --> 00:29:34.435
It is perfectly possible
within our lifetimes,

00:29:34.435 --> 00:29:36.681
we could see China become the
dominant economy in the world,

00:29:36.681 --> 00:29:39.446
in fact as Elon Musk and
others have shown you don't,

00:29:39.446 --> 00:29:42.512
China only has to sort of
grow at the current rate to

00:29:42.512 --> 00:29:44.667
eventually get that.

00:29:44.667 --> 00:29:48.012
And I think this is one of
the things we should just be

00:29:48.012 --> 00:29:51.694
thinking about is some of the
context we have to have in our

00:29:51.694 --> 00:29:53.361
minds is, let's say

00:29:56.554 --> 00:29:59.162
even if we in America, we in Britain,

00:29:59.162 --> 00:30:02.601
we in the West, managed to
make every single field of

00:30:02.601 --> 00:30:04.101
expertise exactly

00:30:05.470 --> 00:30:07.395
dominated in America by well,

00:30:07.395 --> 00:30:10.750
representing America,
with 13% Black people,

00:30:10.750 --> 00:30:13.775
you know 50% or just over 50% of women,

00:30:13.775 --> 00:30:16.118
no point whatever percent of trans people,

00:30:16.118 --> 00:30:20.451
even if we did all of that,
does America beat China?

00:30:22.532 --> 00:30:24.248
Now that was--

00:30:24.248 --> 00:30:25.963
- Even if we did all
of those lofty things.

00:30:25.963 --> 00:30:27.317
- That would strike me as being

00:30:27.317 --> 00:30:30.316
a really important question to sort out,

00:30:30.316 --> 00:30:33.356
and I can't find people in America enough,

00:30:33.356 --> 00:30:35.331
people willing to think about it,

00:30:35.331 --> 00:30:37.525
but that would be the underlying
thing is whilst we were

00:30:37.525 --> 00:30:40.313
doing all of these strange
things for our past

00:30:40.313 --> 00:30:44.657
and our present, the
only global competitor,

00:30:44.657 --> 00:30:49.240
which has no problem with
racism is currently operating

00:30:50.077 --> 00:30:52.137
concentration camps.

00:30:52.137 --> 00:30:53.480
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:30:53.480 --> 00:30:56.897
- I cite some, I mean, just terrifically,

00:30:57.753 --> 00:31:01.341
awful racist things that modern China

00:31:01.341 --> 00:31:03.933
and the founders of modern
China have said and done.

00:31:03.933 --> 00:31:05.358
And again,

00:31:05.358 --> 00:31:09.327
I don't think one in a
million Americans knows this.

00:31:09.327 --> 00:31:11.864
I don't think one in a million
British people knows it.

00:31:11.864 --> 00:31:16.329
And I just this is the
context we need to operate in.

00:31:16.329 --> 00:31:19.115
- Do we have any of the defenses

00:31:19.115 --> 00:31:22.466
to stop the encroachment of China

00:31:22.466 --> 00:31:25.278
or stop that they will be the superpower

00:31:25.278 --> 00:31:27.078
and you know even just in,

00:31:27.078 --> 00:31:29.604
in the last couple days, Joe Biden said,

00:31:29.604 --> 00:31:30.993
there's new world order coming,

00:31:30.993 --> 00:31:32.372
and something to the effect of,

00:31:32.372 --> 00:31:34.955
maybe we'll be in charge of it.

00:31:36.237 --> 00:31:37.832
- I've said for many years

00:31:37.832 --> 00:31:42.243
if you didn't like the era of
so called American hegemony,

00:31:42.243 --> 00:31:45.382
you're gonna love the China's era.

00:31:45.382 --> 00:31:47.312
I have a human rights complaint,

00:31:47.312 --> 00:31:48.750
you'll tell the CCP.

00:31:48.750 --> 00:31:49.583
- Yeah, they'll love that.

00:31:49.583 --> 00:31:50.427
- How interesting.

00:31:50.427 --> 00:31:51.260
- Yeah.

00:31:51.260 --> 00:31:52.093
- How interesting that--

00:31:52.093 --> 00:31:53.139
- They've special rooms for people like us

00:31:53.139 --> 00:31:54.012
I'd assume.

00:31:54.012 --> 00:31:55.459
- Please step this way,

00:31:55.459 --> 00:31:56.292
- Its a--

00:31:56.292 --> 00:32:00.459
- I mean it's really it
feel horribly late empire,

00:32:01.393 --> 00:32:02.810
what we're doing.

00:32:04.064 --> 00:32:06.482
- So how do we reverse course on this?

00:32:06.482 --> 00:32:07.438
Or let's say there was,

00:32:07.438 --> 00:32:09.959
if you were advising
Biden or there was a new

00:32:09.959 --> 00:32:12.338
administration, I know it's
not just a political answer,

00:32:12.338 --> 00:32:13.248
I know that.

00:32:13.248 --> 00:32:17.277
